    "compute_imbalance_pct": 17.34,
    "interpretation": "if compute imbalance exceeds token imbalance, ranks are unequal because of how documents were PACKED, not how many tokens they were given - a straggler no token-counting monitor can see",
    "measured": true,
    "model": "attention cost proxied by sum(segment_length^2); constant is meaningless on a CPU toy, the RATIO between ranks is the measurement",
    "not_fixed_here": "balancing composition across ranks means the rank partition stops being `global_index % world_size`, which is exactly the property that makes resumption across a changed world size exact. Fixing this needs a composition-aware partition that is still a pure function of the global index; it is a real design problem, not an oversight.",
